  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "The polynomial $x^2-bx+c$ has two distinct roots, each of which is also a root of $x^3-ax^2+bx-c$. Determine $c$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$c=0$.",
      "worked": "Let the two distinct quadratic roots be $p,q$, and let the remaining cubic root be $r$. By Vieta’s formulas,\n$$\\begin{align*}p+q&=b,\\\\pq&=c,\\\\pq+pr+qr&=b,\\\\pqr&=c.\\end{align*}$$\nSuppose $c\\ne0$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}r&=\\frac{pqr}{pq}\\\\&=\\frac{c}{c}\\\\&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nHence,\n$$\\begin{align*}b&=pq+pr+qr\\\\&=pq+r(p+q)\\\\&=c+b.\\end{align*}$$\nThis gives $c=0$, contradicting $c\\ne0$. Therefore, $c=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 95
  },
